            "body": "Hi @Asthenia0412, thanks for working on this! I'd been looking at the same issue and noticed a couple of things that might be worth considering:\n\n**ModelOpt NVFP4 + Marlin on Blackwell.** Since `initialize_fp4_gemm_config()` is global, this change also applies to ModelOpt NVFP4. `ModelOptFp4LinearMethod.process_weights_after_loading` currently allows `--fp4-gemm-backend marlin` on any GPU (the `is_marlin()` branch runs before the `is_blackwell` check), so with this PR a ModelOpt user on B200 who explicitly passes `marlin` would get CuteDSL instead. The Marlin kernel itself is only gated on SM80+, so the warning \"FP4 Marlin does not support SM100+\" might be misleading.\n\n**A possibly narrower fix.** Now that #40022 is merged, `_get_scheme_from_parts` already has a weight-only Marlin fallback for W4A4 NVFP4 checkpoints. It's only taken when the capability check fails, so something like this might fix the crash without affecting other quant methods:\n\n```python\nif is_fp4a4_nvfp4_supported and not get_fp4_gemm_runner_backend().is_marlin():\n    return CompressedTensorsW4A4Fp4()\n# otherwise fall through to the existing weight-only Marlin fallback\n```\n\n(The fallback's warning text would need a tweak for the explicit-request case.) `test_compressed_tensors_fp4_schemes.py` already mocks capability and platform, so SM100 + `marlin` cases could go there.\n\nHappy to help if useful. What do you think?\n",
